<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ electoral office confirms unchanged seat count.</title>
<headline>NZ electoral office confirms unchanged seat count.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand's chief electoral office confirmed on Friday that the final seat count from the October 12 general election was unchanged after counting of special votes.</p>
<p>The conservative National Party won 44 seats, Labour 37, nationalist New Zealand First 17, the left-wing Alliance 13, radical free-market Act New Zealand eight and the centrist United Party one.</p>
